<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5318" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bĭformis</span></b> , e, adj.
		bis-forma, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>double</i> or <i>two-formed</i>, <i>two-shaped</i> (<b>poet.</b> or in
			postAug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">proles biformis Minotaurus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 25</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scyllae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 6, 286</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 8, 156</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Janus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. F.
					1, 89</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">5, 424</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(Hermaphroditus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					4, 387</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pater, i. e. Chiron,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 2, 664</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nessus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 9, 121</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hodites,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 12, 456</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">monstrum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 8, 156</span></i>
			: a  Centaur, <i><span class="en">id. Am. 2,
				12, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Claud. in Rufin. 1,
			329</span></i> (cf. biformatus): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pan,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					10, 427</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Glaucus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Rapt. Pros. 3, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cecrops,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just.
					2, 6, 7</span></i>
			.—<b>Trop.</b>, of a poet (as man
			and swan): vates, * <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 2,
				20, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">biformes hominum partus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 12, 64</span></i>
			.</div>
